{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116686","id":3317535405,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7FvZKt","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116686","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116686.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116686.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116686","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116686/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116686/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116686/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1432fb8a752ba9f797c904c115c72e9b049fa859","number":116686,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Allow user defined blend modes for shaders","user":{"login":"erodozer","id":316728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjcyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer","html_url":"https://github.com/erodozer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR an alternative to #102366 that fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2621.  I originally detailed the approach in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102366#issuecomment-3902463409\r\n\r\nAs opposed to exposing new keywords and the details of blend factors entirely within the shaders, users are able to define new blend modes with defined factors.\r\n\r\nThis is accomplished by lifting [RDPipelineColorBlendStateAttachment](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/classes/class_rdpipelinecolorblendstateattachment.html) up to be a more pivotal struct used to define render modes for use in shaders.  A central registry where all existing blend factor settings has been established, and all hard coded blend modes have been relocated to it.  This registry is persisted within MaterialStorage, as the blend factor configurations are slightly different between GLES and Forward renderers.  User visible functions for registering new blend modes is exposed through RenderingServer.  The registry holds the configurations for canvas item, spatial, and texture blit render modes.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nExample of direct blending shader that fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113513\r\n\r\nThe ergonomics are a little awkward versus #102366 because registering a new render mode has to be done incredibly early in the application lifecycle.  This can be accomplished with an Autoload with a static initializer, allowing the blend mode to be registered before any resources are referenced which would trigger a shader compilation.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n# autoload_register_blend.gd\r\n\r\n@tool\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\nstatic func _static_init():\r\n\tvar attachment = RDPipelineColorBlendStateAttachment.new()\r\n\tattachment.enable_blend = true\r\n\tattachment.alpha_blend_op = RenderingDevice.BLEND_OP_ADD\r\n\tattachment.color_blend_op = RenderingDevice.BLEND_OP_ADD\r\n\tattachment.src_alpha_blend_factor = RenderingDevice.BLEND_FACTOR_ONE\r\n\tattachment.dst_alpha_blend_factor = RenderingDevice.BLEND_FACTOR_ONE\r\n\tattachment.src_color_blend_factor = RenderingDevice.BLEND_FACTOR_ONE\r\n\tattachment.dst_color_blend_factor = RenderingDevice.BLEND_FACTOR_ONE\r\n\t\r\n\tRenderingServer.register_blend_mode(\r\n\t\tRenderingServer.SHADER_CANVAS_ITEM,\r\n\t\t\"direct\",\r\n\t\tattachment\r\n\t)\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n# direct_shader.gdshader\r\n\r\nshader_type canvas_item;\r\nrender_mode blend_direct, unshaded;\r\n\r\ninstance uniform vec4 channel : source_color = vec4(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0);\r\n\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n\tvec4 c = texture(TEXTURE, UV);\r\n\tCOLOR = c.a * channel;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1800\" height=\"1247\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d616dccd-52c2-4d8d-ab45-8d23fdc15680\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url"